  "context": "## One Function or Many? The Case For and Against Unified AI Integrity Management\nTwo earlier pieces in this series have laid out the conceptual and institutional case. AI Integrity: a Critical Frontier argued that AI integrity is becoming to intelligent systems what cybersecurity became to software. The Case for AI Integrity Management as a Formal Enterprise Function mapped the landscape of existing disciplines — ethics, compliance, cybersecurity, operational reliability — and argued that the structural logic of convergence is real. This third paper asks whether a unified function is desirable in principle and achievable in practice. Would a unified AI Integrity Management function produce genuine operational benefits, or would it mostly be a reorganisation on paper — the same specialists doing the same work under a new letterhead?\nEtiquetas: Autoridad, permisos y delegación 7.69%; Decisiones y responsabilidad 7.69%; Empresa y gestión 42.31%; Integridad y seguridad de IA 42.31%\nFicha: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/one-function-or-many-the-case-for-and-against-unified-ai-integrity-management-t886/\nDocumento de origen: https://tegrity.ai/one-function-or-many-the-case-for-and-against-unified-ai-integrity-management/\n\n",
